 "answer": "In the LlamaIndex starter tutorial, the index is saved with:\n\n```python\nindex.storage_context.persist()\n```\n\nWith no arguments, `persist()` writes to the default directory **`./storage`**, relative to the current working directory. You can pass a different location with `persist(persist_dir=\"...\")`. To reload the index later, the tutorial uses `StorageContext.from_defaults(persist_dir=\"./storage\")` together with `load_index_from_storage`.\n\nI'm recalling this from the docs and may be missing details for your installed version, so check the current starter tutorial if the code differs.",
